/*
 * The nRF54L15 SoC-default MCUboot partition is 64 KiB, but the FPROTECT
 * hardware on this device can protect at most a single 62 KiB region. With
 * static (devicetree) partitions and MCUboot enabled, that 64 KiB partition
 * makes MCUboot fail to build: "Can not FPROTECT region that big".
 *
 * Shrink the MCUboot partition to 60 KiB (FPROTECT block unit is 1 KiB, so
 * this is valid and below the 62 KiB cap). slot0/slot1/storage are left at
 * their defaults; a 4 KiB gap is left between mcuboot and image-0. This
 * overlay must match the one applied to the MCUboot image under
 * sysbuild/mcuboot/boards/.
 */
&boot_partition {
	reg = <0x0 DT_SIZE_K(60)>;
};
